cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
message: >-
  If you use NSRW, cite this software together with the exact Git commit or
  published release you used. Mathematical execution receipts retain their
  own fixed checkpoints; the software release is not a new proof execution.
title: Navier–Stokes Research Workbench
authors:
  - family-names: Yun
    given-names: Kwansub
repository-code: https://github.com/flamehaven01/NavierStokes-Research-Workbench
url: https://github.com/flamehaven01/NavierStokes-Research-Workbench
license: MIT
version: 0.5.0
abstract: >-
  A research workbench for construction-specific, source-linked formal
  consequences and reproducible bounded checks. The P2 study establishes a
  first-repair mass zero and strictly positive angular history at the same
  point for sufficiently small positive parameters of each fixed source
  Profile. It does not claim general Navier–Stokes correctness, literature
  novelty, independent reproduction or practical solver readiness.
keywords:
  - Navier–Stokes
  - Lean
  - formalization
  - reproducibility
